window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"models-and-trusted-access\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">模型与可信访问</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本的文档。</p> </blockquote> <p>OpenAI Daybreak 面向获准用户，帮助他们开展经过授权的防御性网络安全工作。Daybreak Blue 可在获准的防御性工作流程中提供旗舰模型的使用权限，并减少此类工作流中的拒绝响应。Daybreak Red 则须经过单独审批，可用于更高级安全研究的专业网络安全模型。</p> <p>请将获准使用的模型与受控环境、对获准系统和操作的明确限制、最小权限以及敏感操作执行前的自动审查结合使用。模型只能通过获准的身份、工作区或 API 组织与项目，以及获准的产品界面使用。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-right-model\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择合适的模型</h2> <p>大多数经过授权的防御性工作可先使用 <strong>GPT-Daybreak-Blue</strong>。此模型面向防御性安全工作提供先进能力，并减少相关工作流中的拒绝响应，包括：</p> <ul> <li>发现漏洞并进行分类处理。</li> <li>安全代码审查和威胁建模。</li> <li>检测工程和事件响应。</li> <li>在受控环境中分析恶意软件。</li> <li>修复问题并验证补丁。</li> </ul> <p><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Red</strong> 是专业网络安全模型，用于须单独获批且经过明确授权的工作流程，例如在受控条件下复现漏洞、开展概念验证（proof-of-concept，PoC）或漏洞利用（exploit）验证、进行渗透测试、红队测试以及复杂系统分析。它不是日常安全工作的默认选择，且不会自动获得访问权限，也并非所有产品界面都提供此模型。</p> <p>这些高级工作流程可能与恶意活动相似，因此必须有明确授权。只有在你拥有相关系统或获准评估这些系统时，才能通过获批的模型和产品界面开展工作，并应保持适当的人工监督。</p> <p>例如：</p> <ul> <li><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Blue：</strong> 检查获准的实验环境代码仓库，查找身份验证方面的弱点；依据证据和影响对发现进行排序；提出补丁，但不访问外部系统。</li> <li><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Red：</strong> 在获准的实验环境和测试时段内复现已记录的身份验证缺陷，验证最小化概念验证；在访问凭据、建立持久化或更改生产环境之前停止。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"trusted-access-for-cyber\">网络安全可信访问计划（Trusted Access for Cyber）</h2> <p>请通过 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001258-trusted-access-for-cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trusted Access for Cyber（需联网）</a> 申请 <strong>Daybreak 访问权限</strong>。能否访问取决于是否已针对你的特定身份或服务、ChatGPT 工作区或 API 组织与项目、获准的服务和模型，以及允许使用的产品界面完成审批和开通。</p> <ul> <li>个人可通过<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">个人 Trusted Access 申请（需联网）</a>申请访问。</li> <li>组织可提交<a href=\"https://openai.com/form/enterprise-trusted-access-for-cyber/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">企业 Trusted Access 申请表（需联网）</a>，并与自己的 OpenAI 代表协调。</li> </ul> <p>提交申请或完成身份验证，不代表一定会获批。</p> <p>申请、完成身份验证或获批 Daybreak Blue，<strong>都不会</strong>授予 Daybreak Red 或 GPT-Daybreak-Red 的访问权。专业服务必须单独审批和开通。</p> <p>对于企业访问权限，只能在获准的工作区、API 组织或项目中开展本组织获准的内部工作。不得将其扩展给外部用户或第三方客户，不得用于对外提供的服务、下游产品功能，也不得用于获准范围之外的系统。如果获准使用的身份、工作区、API 组织、项目、模型或产品界面不明确，请先暂停并向 OpenAI 代表确认。</p> <p>Trusted Access 不会自动授予<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">零数据保留</a>权限。开始工作前，请确认针对确切 API 组织和适用端点，是否另行批准了相应的数据保留控制措施。</p> <p><a id=\"false-positives\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">误报</h2> <p>合法的网络安全活动或其他无关活动仍可能触发安全防护。如果安全措施阻止、转交或限制了请求，请检查客户端显示的通知和请求日志。详情、需要收集的信息及后续步骤，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001259\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">常见问题与故障排除（需联网）</a>。如果怀疑 Codex 误报，可在有此功能时通过 <code>/feedback</code> 报告。对于 API 访问限制及申诉，请遵循 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/safety-checks/cybersecurity.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 网络安全检查指南</a>。</p> <p>所有用户仍须遵守<a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/usage-policies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用政策（需联网）</a>和<a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/row-terms-of-use/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用条款（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-your-security-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">配置安全工作流程</h2> <p>Trusted Access 管理获准的模型访问权限，但不会替你配置环境、强制实施获准系统和操作的限制，也不会审查拟执行的操作。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b74b7c76c711106d\">使用建议配置</a>，设置隔离环境、最小权限、明确的边界，以及针对敏感操作的防护措施。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"models-and-trusted-access\">Models and Trusted Access</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>OpenAI Daybreak helps approved users perform authorized defensive cybersecurity work. Daybreak Blue provides access to flagship models with reduced refusals for authorized defensive workflows. Daybreak Red provides separately approved access to specialist cyber models for more advanced security research.</p> <p>Combine your approved model with a controlled environment, clear limits on approved systems and actions, least-privilege permissions, and automatic review before sensitive actions run. Use the model only with the approved identity, workspace or API organization and project, and product surface.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-right-model\">Choose the right model</h2> <p>Start with <strong>GPT-Daybreak-Blue</strong> for most authorized defensive work. This model provides access to advanced capabilities with reduced refusals for defensive security workflows, including:</p> <ul> <li>Vulnerability discovery and triage.</li> <li>Secure code review and threat modeling.</li> <li>Detection engineering and incident response.</li> <li>Malware analysis in a controlled environment.</li> <li>Remediation and patch validation.</li> </ul> <p><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Red</strong> is a specialist cyber model for separately approved, explicitly authorized workflows, such as controlled vulnerability reproduction, proof-of-concept or exploit validation, penetration testing, red teaming, and complex system analysis. It isn't the default choice for routine security work, and access isn't available automatically or on every surface.</p> <p>These advanced workflows can resemble malicious activity without clear authorization. Use the approved model and surface only for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess, and keep appropriate human oversight in place.</p> <p>For example:</p> <ul> <li><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Blue:</strong> Review the approved lab repository for authentication weaknesses, rank findings by evidence and impact, and propose patches without accessing external systems.</li> <li><strong>GPT-Daybreak-Red:</strong> Within the approved lab and testing window, reproduce the documented authentication flaw, validate a minimal proof of concept, and stop before credential access, persistence, or production changes.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"trusted-access-for-cyber\">Trusted Access for Cyber</h2> <p>Request <strong>Daybreak access</strong> through <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001258-trusted-access-for-cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trusted Access for Cyber (online)</a>. Access depends on approval and provisioning for your specific identity or service, ChatGPT workspace or API organization and project, authorized offering and model, and allowed product surface.</p> <ul> <li>Individuals can request access through the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">individual Trusted Access application (online)</a>.</li> <li>Organizations can submit the <a href=\"https://openai.com/form/enterprise-trusted-access-for-cyber/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">enterprise Trusted Access request form (online)</a> and coordinate with their OpenAI representative.</li> </ul> <p>Submitting an application or completing identity verification doesn't guarantee approval.</p> <p>Applying, verifying your identity, or receiving approval for Daybreak Blue doesn't grant access to Daybreak Red or GPT-Daybreak-Red. The specialist offering requires separate approval and provisioning.</p> <p>For enterprise access, use the approved workspace, API organization, or project only for your organization's authorized internal work. Don't extend it to external users, third-party customers, externally offered services, downstream product features, or systems outside the approved work. If the approved identity, workspace, API organization, project, model, or surface is unclear, stop and confirm it with your OpenAI representative.</p> <p>Trusted Access doesn't automatically grant <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Zero Data Retention</a>. Confirm any separately approved retention controls for the exact API organization and applicable endpoint before you begin.</p> <h2 id=\"false-positives\">False positives</h2> <p>Legitimate cybersecurity or unrelated activity can still trigger a safeguard. If a safeguard blocks, reroutes, or limits a request, inspect the available client notice and request logs. Review <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001259\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Common Issues and Troubleshooting (online)</a> for details to collect and next steps. Report suspected Codex false positives through <code>/feedback</code> when available. For API access restrictions and appeals, follow the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/safety-checks/cybersecurity.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API cybersecurity checks guidance</a>.</p> <p>All users remain subject to the <a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/usage-policies/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Usage Policies (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/row-terms-of-use/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Terms of Use (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-your-security-workflow\">Configure your security workflow</h2> <p>Trusted Access governs approved model access, but it doesn't configure your environment, enforce limits on approved systems and actions, or review proposed actions.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b74b7c76c711106d\">Use the recommended configuration</a> for isolation, least-privilege permissions, clearly defined boundaries, and guardrails for sensitive actions.</li> </ul>"};
